    "shufflenetv2_x0_5": 1.0,
    "mbv3_large_320": 1.0
   },
   "tolerance": "float32 SIMD reassociation only; no model was retrained or fine-tuned"
  },
  "fidelity": "With correct input normalisation P1 is a genuine approximation (cosine ~0.6-0.7 at a ~40% MAC cut) and P2 is exact on static content and increasingly approximate under motion; the numbers below are what the kernels actually produce.",
  "p2_caveat": "On the near-static R1 stream P2 has almost no true motion to exploit, so its fidelity is high; under fast motion, illumination steps and scene cuts the ghosting is visible in spatial_rel_l2 and is reported instead of averaged away",
  "mask_note": "The tile statistic was already a mean over the 12 channel values in every published run; the 100%-flush behaviour seen on real footage came from receptive-field percolation (one 8-neighbour dilation plus an any-dirty-tile footprint rule saturates a 7x7 deep grid from ~11% scattered tiles), not from a max-pixel statistic. See docs/CM_CNN_ACCELERATION.md section 15.8"
